<?php declare(strict_types=1); ?><!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="UTF-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1.0"><meta name="description" content="Project Unveiled presents Truth on Trial, powered by the Trust-Worthy investigation method. Question everything, inspect the evidence, and you be the judge."><title>Project Unveiled | Truth on Trial</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/truth/truth-worthy.css"></head><body><header class="topbar"><div class="wrap nav"><a class="brand" href="/truth/">PROJECT UNVEILED <span>TRUTH ON TRIAL</span></a><nav class="navlinks"><a href="#daily">Daily Truth Trial</a><a href="#trials">Truth Trials</a><a href="#ask">Ask a Question</a><a href="/book/research.html">Research Standards</a></nav></div></header><main><section class="hero"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">PROJECT UNVEILED · TRUTH ON TRIAL · POWERED BY TRUST-WORTHY</div><h1>QUESTION EVERYTHING!</h1><p>Truth on Trial starts with the question, not the approved answer. Powered by the Trust-Worthy method, we trace claims toward the underlying record, question the source behind the source, test motives and incentives, hunt contradictions and counterevidence, apply logic and common sense, and show our reasoning.</p><div class="manifesto"><strong>We do not tell you what to think.</strong> We show what is proven, what is strongly indicated, what does not add up, what remains unknown, and—when useful—our clearly labeled Bobinated Opinion with the logic behind it. <strong>You be the judge.</strong></div></div></section><section class="section" id="daily"><div class="wrap"><article class="card daily-desk"><div class="eyebrow">Truth on Trial · Daily Desk</div><h2>Today’s claims go on trial.</h2><p>Major news, official statements, public posts, viral claims, propaganda, conspiracy claims, corporate narratives, scientific controversies, religious claims, and historical claims can all be examined under the same rule: <strong>QUESTION EVERYTHING.</strong></p><p class="muted">The daily desk identifies the factual propositions people are being asked to accept, traces them toward primary or earliest accessible evidence, tests the strongest competing explanations, and publishes what survives. The investigation is the product—not copied news content.</p><div class="finding"><strong>Recurring close:</strong> Here is the claim. Here is what we found. Here is what supports it, what cuts against it, what appears most likely, and what we still cannot establish. <strong>YOU BE THE JUDGE.</strong></div></article></div></section><section class="section" id="trials"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">Published & Open Investigations</div><h2>Truth Trials</h2><div class="grid"><article class="card"><div class="case-head"><div><div class="case-id">TW-CLAIM-000001</div><h2>Does God individually cause or permit every bad thing?</h2></div><div class="status">PROVISIONAL</div></div><p>The evidence does not require the conclusion that every harmful event is individually caused or separately permitted by God. But the opposite absolute—“God is not in control”—also outruns the evidence.</p><div class="finding"><strong>What survived:</strong> the biblical material holds divine sovereignty, human agency, ordinary causation, and hostile spiritual agency in tension rather than reducing every tragedy to one simple mechanism.</div><p><a class="button" href="/truth/case-000001.php">Read the Full Investigation</a></p></article><article class="card"><div class="case-head"><div><div class="case-id">TW-CLAIM-000002</div><h2>Did Jesus teach the modern Romans Road / sinner's prayer?</h2></div><div class="status">OPEN</div></div><p>Truth on Trial puts a familiar evangelical salvation formula on trial: Jesus' recorded teaching, Romans itself, conversion history, and the strongest defense of the modern practice.</p><div class="finding"><strong>First-pass finding:</strong> the standardized method appears to be a later evangelistic framework built from genuine New Testament material—not a formula recorded on Jesus' lips.</div><p><a class="button" href="/truth/case-000002.php">Examine Case 000002</a></p></article></div></div></section><section class="section"><div class="wrap"><article class="card"><div class="eyebrow">Every Full Case</div><h2>The reader should be able to see the whole trail.</h2><div class="case-anatomy"><div class="anatomy-item"><strong>1. The Claim</strong><span>What proposition are we actually testing?</span></div><div class="anatomy-item"><strong>2. What’s Proven</strong><span>Facts directly established by the available record.</span></div><div class="anatomy-item"><strong>3. Strongly Indicated</strong><span>What the total pattern points toward without pretending it is proven.</span></div><div class="anatomy-item"><strong>4. Contradictions</strong><span>Missing pieces, conflicts, omissions, and counterevidence.</span></div><div class="anatomy-item"><strong>5. Motives / Incentives</strong><span>Who benefits, who pays, who controls, and what interests matter. Motive is context, not proof.</span></div><div class="anatomy-item"><strong>6. Logic & Common Sense</strong><span>Do the premises hold? Does the conclusion follow? Is there a simpler explanation?</span></div><div class="anatomy-item"><strong>7. Unknowns</strong><span>What we cannot responsibly establish yet.</span></div><div class="anatomy-item"><strong>8. Bobinated Opinion</strong><span>Our clearly labeled reasoned opinion—what appears most likely and exactly why.</span></div><div class="anatomy-item"><strong>9. YOU BE THE JUDGE</strong><span>Inspect the trail and reach your own conclusion.</span></div></div></article></div></section><section class="section" id="ask"><div class="wrap grid"><article class="card"><div class="eyebrow">Private Question Intake</div><h2>What should go on trial?</h2><p class="muted">Submit a question privately. Truth on Trial reviews it before opening any public investigation. Honest questions are welcome; publication is not automatic.</p><form class="challenge" action="/truth/question-submit.php" method="post"><input type="hidden" name="opened_at" id="questionOpenedAt" value=""><div class="hp" aria-hidden="true"><label>Website<input name="website" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off"></label></div><div class="row"><div><label for="topic">Topic</label><select id="topic" name="topic" required><option value="">Choose one</option><option value="news">News / public claim</option><option value="propaganda">Propaganda / viral narrative</option><option value="jesus">Jesus / Gospel</option><option value="doctrine">Doctrine / theology</option><option value="history">History / sources</option><option value="science">Science / nature</option><option value="current-events">Current events</option><option value="other">Other</option></select></div><div><label for="questionName">Name or handle (optional)</label><input id="questionName" name="name" maxlength="100" autocomplete="name"></div></div><label for="question">Your question</label><textarea id="question" name="question" minlength="20" maxlength="3000" required></textarea><label for="context">Why does this matter, or what evidence should be considered? (optional)</label><textarea id="context" name="context" maxlength="2000"></textarea><label for="questionEmail">Email for an update (optional)</label><input id="questionEmail" type="email" name="email" maxlength="190" autocomplete="email"><button class="button" type="submit">Put a Question Up for Review</button></form></article><aside class="card"><h3>What happens next</h3><ul class="rules"><li>We clarify the actual claim before investigating it.</li><li>We trace the source and the source behind the source.</li><li>We seek contrary evidence instead of protecting a preferred answer.</li><li>We distinguish proof, strong indication, inference, opinion, and unknowns.</li><li>A serious challenge can revise the public case.</li></ul><div class="judge">YOU BE THE JUDGE.<small>QUESTION EVERYTHING.</small></div></aside></div></section><section class="section"><div class="wrap grid"><article class="card"><div class="eyebrow">The Trust-Worthy Method</div><h2>Investigate before answering.</h2><div class="steps"><div class="step"><div class="num">1</div><div><strong>Define</strong><span>Separate the actual proposition from assumptions hidden inside the question.</span></div></div><div class="step"><div class="num">2</div><div><strong>Trace</strong><span>Follow citations backward toward primary and earliest accessible evidence.</span></div></div><div class="step"><div class="num">3</div><div><strong>Interrogate</strong><span>Question provenance, chronology, funding, incentives, beneficiaries, omissions, and context.</span></div></div><div class="step"><div class="num">4</div><div><strong>Corroborate</strong><span>Separate independent evidence from thousands of repetitions of one source.</span></div></div><div class="step"><div class="num">5</div><div><strong>Attack</strong><span>Build the strongest credible case against the leading explanation.</span></div></div><div class="step"><div class="num">6</div><div><strong>Reason</strong><span>Use logic and common sense while keeping established fact separate from inference.</span></div></div><div class="step"><div class="num">7</div><div><strong>Publish & revise</strong><span>Show the trail, invite challenge, and change the finding when better information wins.</span></div></div></div></article><aside class="card"><h3>The Trial Rules</h3><ul class="rules"><li>No third-party fact-check verdict is treated as authority.</li><li>Primary and earliest accessible evidence receives priority.</li><li>Contrary evidence must be actively sought.</li><li>Motive, money, and power can be examined but are not proof by themselves.</li><li>No hard proof does not mean no reasonable inference.</li><li>A reasonable inference is never relabeled as proven fact.</li><li>Bobinated Opinion is always labeled as opinion and shows its reasoning.</li><li>The Trust-Worthy method itself receives no immunity from challenge.</li></ul><div class="finding"><strong>Powered by Trust-Worthy.</strong><br>The engine investigates. The evidence is shown. You decide.</div></aside></div></section></main><footer class="footer"><div class="wrap"><strong>PROJECT UNVEILED</strong> · Truth on Trial · Powered by Trust-Worthy · <strong>YOU BE THE JUDGE.</strong></div></footer><script>document.getElementById("questionOpenedAt").value=Math.floor(Date.now()/1000);</script></body></html>